  "divergence_resolved": {
    "question": "kill_or_scale 45d = 187 installs / 0 updates vs same cache recomputed = 256 / 434. Which one reads Product Type wrong?",
    "verdict": "kill_or_scale.py reads Product Type WRONG. pull_analytics.py is correct.",
    "decided_by": "reading both sources + enumerating the Product Type values this app actually emits",
    "product_types_actually_emitted_45d": {
      "1F": {
        "rows": 148,
        "units": 183
      },
      "F1": {
        "rows": 70,
        "units": 73
      },
      "F3": {
        "rows": 24,
        "units": 25
      },
      "F7": {
        "rows": 177,
        "units": 434
      }
    },
    "mechanism": [
      "kill_or_scale.py (_GambitStudio/scripts/asc/kill_or_scale.py, lines 124-127) classifies by PREFIX: ptype.startswith('7') -> update, ptype.startswith('1') -> install.",
      "This app emits NO product type starting with '7'. Every update is 'F7'. startswith('7') therefore matches zero rows -> the reported '0 updates' is an artifact of the prefix test, not a fact about the app.",
      "Likewise startswith('1') matches '1F' (183 units) but misses 'F1' (73 units), so installs are under-counted by ~29%. 183 vs the 256 of the exact test; kill_or_scale printed 187 because its window ends at today-1 and it refetches from ASC instead of the cache.",
      "pull_analytics.py (lines 91-92) uses exact set membership INSTALL={'1','1F','1T','F1'} / UPDATE={'7','7F','7T','F7'}, which covers the F-prefixed forms. Its 60d figure (341) matches the independent recompute exactly."
    ],
    "numbers_to_use": "the recompute / pull_analytics figures. 45d = 256 installs 1*, 434 updates 7*, 25 redownloads 3*.",
    "scope_note": "This is a bug in a SHARED lab script (kill_or_scale.py) and affects every app whose Sales rows use the F-prefixed product types. Reported, not fixed here — out of scope for the extractor.",
    "learnings_53": "The learning says 1*/7*; the trap is that '*' is a wildcard on BOTH sides (F1, F7), so a prefix test is not a correct implementation of it."
  }
}